  "body": "## What changed\n\nA Drill, Bore or Thread operation reads the stock when no model is picked as its source. Detect holes then finds nothing, and the old refusal said \"the source model\". That text pointed the user at the wrong thing.\n\nThe three \"nothing found\" refusals of `detect_holes` (drilled holes, Z-axis holes, upright round bosses) now:\n\n- say \"the stock\" when the source is the stock, and \"the source model\" for each other source;\n- add the fix on a stock source: `'D1' reads the stock, not a model: pick a model as the source (source: \"block\" or source: \"disc\")`;\n- say \"import a model and pick it as the source\" when the document has no model.\n\nA model source keeps its old refusal, word for word. The helpers are in a new module, `crates/app/src/operation/detect_source.rs`, because `operation/material.rs` is longer than 400 lines. The decision is in `docs/decisions/3544-detect-holes-stock-source.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- New test `mcp::detect_holes_on_a_stock_source_names_the_stock_and_the_models_to_pick`: no model, two models, and a model source.\n- The existing tests that match the old words still pass (`thread_boss`, `mcp`, the UI test for \"no drilled holes\").\n- `cargo xtask gate quick`: 342 of 343 steps pass. The one failure, `plunge_depth_tab::the_tabbed_contour_catalog_case_names_its_tab_window_dives`, also fails on `main` without this change.\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe Detect holes button in the desktop app was not clicked. It shows the same text as the MCP tool.\n\nChangelog: Detect holes on an operation that reads the stock now says so and names the models to pick as the source.\nEffort: low\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #3544",
